From e8bcfcd53b7e08313fa15f22054af6cedfbf499e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] aggregate copy-forward: real fixes for the 3 blockers
 that kept struct_copy at 3.1x; i686 pair load/store base-clobber miscompile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

IS-02/struct_copy (P0, biggest measured S gap): 'build(tmp); memcpy(dst,
tmp)' forwarding was blocked three separate ways on the canonical
inlined-struct-return shape, so every make_particle still built 48
bytes on the stack and copied them out:

1. STALE PARAM EXCLUSION. forward_store_only_temporaries excluded 'the
   first params.len() entry allocas' as forwarding sources. mem2reg
   deletes promoted scalar param allocas, so the positional count
   excluded the first two TEMPORARIES instead. Use the authoritative
   func.param_alloca_values (kept in sync by lowering/mem2reg/
   tail_call_elim); fall back to the positional rule only when empty
   (inliner-built functions), fail closed.

2. DEST DEFINED TOO LATE. The copy destination is usually the
   'g->particles[i]' GEP emitted right before the memcpy — after the
   temp's first store — and the def-before-first-use ordering check
   rejected it. A const-offset GetElementPtr is pure address
   arithmetic: hoist it above the first root use when its base
   dominates that point (one hoist per run; the driver's fixed-point
   loop handles chains).

3. WINDOW OVER-REJECTION. The dest-liveness window (zlib-ng fold_1
   guard) treated ANY instruction referencing a dest-rooted value as
   touching dest's memory — including the hoisted GEP itself.
   GEP/Copy/Phi only create aliases; actual accesses through them are
   still caught by the paths lookup on the accessing instruction.
   Everything else (Load/Store/Memcpy/Call/...) still fails closed.

struct_copy -O2: 3.11x -> 1.54x vs GCC (83ms -> 41ms); all 4 aggregate
memcpys in the corpus eliminated (was 0 of 4).

i686 CORRECTNESS (exposed by the -m32 battery, PRE-EXISTING on main):
the F64/I64 pair load through SlotAddr::Reg emitted
'movl (%eax),%eax; movl 4(%eax),%edx' when RA homed the pointer in
%eax (Phase 2e accumulator home) — the first load destroys the base,
the second dereferences the loaded LOW WORD (nbody/struct_copy -m32
SIGSEGV). Fixed by ordering the pair so the base register is written
last (load sites, memory.rs 259/513) and by stashing an %eax/%edx base
into the %ecx address scratch before the value pair is staged (store
sites, which cannot reorder because the value occupies both halves).
25-line reproducer: 5-body force loop, bodies[i].vx -= dx*bodies[j].mass.

Validation: 991/991 unit, 50/50 correctness, 46/46 check scripts,
regparm -O0..-Os, x86-64 differential fuzz 147/150 (3 pre-existing
fails, seeds 4/9/100, identical on unmodified main), NEW m32
differential fuzz 200/200, benchmark parity vs gcc -m32/-m64 (nbody,
spectral_norm, binary_trees, struct_copy, hash_table, qsort).
